      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T15:48:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The \u0027intent\u0027 may record the operation as \u0027index\u0027, but the change may be deleted by the time recover() is called for its intent. Or, vice versa, intent records operation as delete, but the notedb delete fails for some reason, and our recover will endup deleting the change from the index. So, instead of relying on the recorded operation, should we directly check notedb here to derive the operation?",
